# Line endings are pinned per file type, so a checkout produces the same bytes on
# every machine no matter what core.autocrlf says. Everything else keeps following
# core.autocrlf, as before.
#
# .sh/.py must be LF: with a CRLF checkout the \r lands inside the "#!/bin/sh"
# shebang and at the end of every command, and sh on Linux aborts with
# "bad interpreter" / "command not found". These run on Astra, not through MSYS,
# which reads scripts in text mode and hides the damage.
#
# .bat/.cmd must be CRLF: cmd.exe is unhappy with labels and goto in an LF-only
# batch file.
*.sh	text eol=lf
*.py	text eol=lf
*.bat	text eol=crlf
*.cmd	text eol=crlf
